The legal text is the Constitution of the Independent State of Papua New Guinea as published by the National
Parliament of Papua New Guinea (https://parliament.gov.pg/constitution-of-png/), a consolidated reprint of the
Office of Legislative Counsel, read on 29 October 2026. The page carries no licence statement. The text is
reproduced as an official publication of the Parliament, with attribution to it.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and are dedicated
to the public domain under CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). This repository is not legal advice and not an official
publication.

Further legal texts, each credited in its commit (Source, Source-status): Rules of Court as published by the
PNG Judiciary (https://www.pngjudiciary.gov.pg; no licence statement; official texts of the Rules Committee);
Acts as certified, published by the National Parliament (https://pdis.parliament.gov.pg; no licence statement;
official texts); secondary copies of PNG Acts and regulations from WIPO Lex (https://www.wipo.int/wipolex;
terms of use https://www.wipo.int/tools/en/disclaim.html) and FAOLEX (https://faolex.fao.org; FAO terms: reuse
with credit to FAO/FAOLEX, https://www.fao.org/contact-us/terms/en/). Under the Copyright and Neighbouring
Rights Act 2000, section 5(b), official texts of a legislative, administrative or legal nature are not
protected.

Further official texts, from 27 November 2026, each credited in its commit: Civil Aviation Rules as
consolidated by the Civil Aviation Safety Authority (https://casapng.gov.pg); Acts, regulations, rules,
determinations and orders published by NICTA (https://www.nicta.gov.pg), the ICCC (https://iccc.gov.pg), the
Departments of Treasury (https://treasury.gov.pg), Finance (https://www.finance.gov.pg) and ICT
(https://www.ict.gov.pg), the Mineral Resources Authority (https://www.mra.gov.pg), the Ombudsman Commission
(https://ombudsman.gov.pg), the Department of the Prime Minister and NEC (https://pmnec.gov.pg), the
Investment Promotion Authority (https://www.ipa.gov.pg), PNG Customs (https://customs.gov.pg) and the National
Court election petitions registry (https://www.pngep.com), none with a licence statement; Acts as certified
from the former parliament.gov.pg Acts folder, read from the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org;
archive.org terms https://archive.org/about/terms.php) because the address no longer answers; commencement
days from the Office of Legislative Counsel's tables (https://www.pnglaw.gov.pg). All are official texts of a
legislative, administrative or legal nature, not protected under section 5(b) of the Copyright and
Neighbouring Rights Act 2000.
